<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">756–812</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Ibrahim ibn al-Aghlab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab was an Arab army commander who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. In 800 the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a> made him hereditary governor of the province in return for an annual tribute, giving his family virtual independence. He restored order among the restless Arab troops and built the palace city of al-Abbasiyya near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-i-ibn-al-aghlab.jpg" alt="Ibrahim I ibn al-Aghlab" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aghlabid_dirham_-_Ibrahim_ibn_al-Aghlab_-_al-Maamoun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
